## 🏃 Dry Run

### Example 1

**Input:**

```text
nums = [0, 1, 0, 3, 12]
```

Initially:

```text
j = 0
```

### First loop: Move non-zero elements

| `i` | `nums[i]` | Action              | `j` after action |
| --: | --------: | ------------------- | ---------------: |
|   0 |         0 | Skip zero           |                0 |
|   1 |         1 | Place 1 at index 0  |                1 |
|   2 |         0 | Skip zero           |                1 |
|   3 |         3 | Place 3 at index 1  |                2 |
|   4 |        12 | Place 12 at index 2 |                3 |

After the first loop:

```text
[1, 3, 12, 3, 12]
```

**Important:** The last two positions still contain old values. We will overwrite them with zeros in the second loop.

### Second loop: Fill zeros

Since `j = 3`, start at index `3`.

| Index | Action   | Array               |
| ----: | -------- | ------------------- |
|     3 | Set to 0 | `[1, 3, 12, 0, 12]` |
|     4 | Set to 0 | `[1, 3, 12, 0, 0]`  |

**Final output:**

```text
[1, 3, 12, 0, 0]
```

